## 2026-06-07 - US-003
- What was implemented: Added `app.post('/internal/full-content/items/:id')` route to the DO router immediately after `/internal/blurhash/items/:id`. Added `type FullContentStatus` to the import from shared/schema.js. The handler validates the id (integer >= 1) and the status against ALL_FULL_CONTENT_STATUSES, returns 400 on invalid input, writes full_content + full_content_fetched_at + full_content_status when html is non-empty, writes only full_content_fetched_at + full_content_status on failure, calls bumpFeedVersion(), and returns 204. Created test/store-full-content-endpoint.ts (7 tests, node-platform) and registered it in test/run-all-tests.mjs.
- Files changed: src/server/durable-objects/index.ts, test/store-full-content-endpoint.ts (new), test/run-all-tests.mjs, specs/prd.json
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - The DO's createSql mock must handle `UPDATE user_state SET feed_version` for bumpFeedVersion; the SQL mock pattern in test/fetch-full-endpoint.ts does NOT handle it (since that endpoint does not call bumpFeedVersion), so new tests for routes that call bumpFeedVersion need to add it to the mock.
  - Node-platform test registration: add an esbuild entry to run-all-tests.mjs under the "node-platform tests" section, mirroring the fetch-full-endpoint.ts pattern.
---

## 2026-06-07 - US-004
- What was implemented: Created src/server/article-fetch-consumer.ts exporting `handleArticleFetchQueueBatch(batch, env, deps)` and `createArticleFetchConsumerDeps()`. The consumer validates each message with `isArticleFetchJob`, acks invalid jobs immediately, calls `deps.fetchArticle(link)` for valid jobs, POSTs the result JSON to `/internal/full-content/items/:id` on the USER_DO stub (throws if not ok), then acks on success. A TODO comment marks the placeholder for body-blur enqueue (US-012). Created test/article-fetch-consumer.ts (3 tests, node-platform): one DO write on success, invalid job ack, failure status forwarded and acked. Registered in test/run-all-tests.mjs.
- Files changed: src/server/article-fetch-consumer.ts (new), test/article-fetch-consumer.ts (new), test/run-all-tests.mjs, specs/prd.json
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - The consumer pattern exactly mirrors blurhash-consumer.ts: QueueMessageLike/QueueBatchLike interfaces, invalid body → immediate ack, transient failures (non-ok DO response) → throw (queue retry), permanent failures → ack.
  - `createArticleFetchConsumerDeps()` just wraps `fetchFullArticle` from article-fetch.ts; the deps interface keeps tests hermetic.
  - The TODO comment for US-012 is in `handleArticleFetchMessage`, just before the `writeFullContent` call.
---


## 2026-06-07 - US-005
- What was implemented: Created src/server/article-prefetch-eligible.ts exporting `isPrefetchEligible(item)` which returns false when `full_content` is present, otherwise delegates to `isSummaryOnly`. Created test/article-prefetch-eligible.ts (4 browser tests) covering: eligible summary-only, not-eligible (no link), not-eligible (long body), not-eligible (has full_content). Registered the test in test/browser-tests.ts. Added a private `enqueueArticleFetches(items)` method to the DO that guards on `env.ARTICLE_FETCH_QUEUE`, queries `content/description/full_content` per item from SQLite, checks `isPrefetchEligible`, and sends an `ArticleFetchJob` for eligible items. Called right after `await this.updateNewItemThumbnails(newItems)`. Added imports for `isPrefetchEligible` and `ArticleFetchJob` to the DO file.
- Files changed: src/server/article-prefetch-eligible.ts (new), test/article-prefetch-eligible.ts (new), test/browser-tests.ts, src/server/durable-objects/index.ts, specs/prd.json
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - `isPrefetchEligible` is a thin wrapper: short-circuit on `full_content` truthy, then delegate to `isSummaryOnly` from shared/article-detect.ts. No need to duplicate the threshold logic.
  - The DO method queries `content, description, full_content` per item individually from SQLite (not a bulk query) to keep the loop readable. For large batches a JOIN would be faster but new items typically arrive in single digits.
  - `this.ctx.id.toString()` gives the DO objectId needed by ArticleFetchJob.
---

## 2026-06-07 - US-006
- What was implemented: Modified `worker.queue` in `src/server/index.ts` to branch on `batch.queue.startsWith('article-fetch-jobs')`. When true, dynamically imports `article-fetch-consumer.js` and calls `handleArticleFetchQueueBatch` with `createArticleFetchConsumerDeps()`. The else branch keeps the existing blurhash routing via `blurhash-runtime.js`.
- Files changed: src/server/index.ts, specs/prd.json
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - The dynamic import destructuring must use object-curly-newline style (multi-line braces) to satisfy the eslint `object-curly-newline` rule enforced in this project.
  - `batch.queue` is the queue name string on `MessageBatch`; `startsWith('article-fetch-jobs')` covers both dev and prod queue names.
---

## 2026-06-07 - US-007
- What was implemented: Added `full_content_images TEXT` column to the items table schema, DO migration v7, ITEM_COLUMNS, client ensureItemFullContentColumns, upsertItem, and Item type.
- Files changed: src/shared/schema.ts, src/server/durable-objects/index.ts, src/client/db/pull-sync.ts, src/client/db/types.ts, specs/prd.json, test/pull-sync.ts
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - Adding a new column follows the same four-file pattern: schema.ts CREATE TABLE, DO migration + ITEM_COLUMNS, pull-sync.ts ensureItemFullContentColumns + upsertItem (both bodySetClause branches, INSERT list, VALUES placeholder, bind array), types.ts Item interface.
  - The DO migration version must be bumped whenever a new PRAGMA-guarded ALTER TABLE migration is added; the migration runner checks `migration_v !== USER_DO_MIGRATION_VERSION` and re-runs all migrations on mismatch (they are idempotent).
